I was wondering what your take would be on those issues.

252
00:12:38,939 --> 00:12:40,699
Thanks again for publishing the website.

253
00:12:40,699 --> 00:12:42,579
I have spent untold hours

254
00:12:42,579 --> 00:12:45,100
researching this type of thing all over the web

255
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:46,740
all we know to find it consolidated

256
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:48,500
into one really useful site.

257
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,420
Well, Scott, thanks for your kind words

258
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:51,900
and thanks for getting in touch.

259
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:54,340
Sounds like, as a new scout master,

260
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:57,340
you're making things happen, and good on you for that.

261
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:59,060
You're right about the senior patrol leader.

262
00:12:59,060 --> 00:13:00,900
The senior patrol leader

263
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:03,100
appoints the quarter master and the scribe

264
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,060
and things like that.

265
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:05,700
You know. of course, the patrol leaders

266
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,740
are elected by the scouts and their patrol

267
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,740
And that's straight out of the scout master handbook.

268
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:12,100
So why anybody would be pushing you on that one,

269
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:14,180
You know? I don't know what their beef would be

270
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:15,020
about that.

271
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:16,580
And I think if you pointed out to them

272
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:17,740
in the scout master handbook,

273
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:19,380
maybe they'll change their minds.

274
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:20,740
And if they don't change their minds,

275
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:21,700
point it out to them and say

276
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:25,380
this is what we're doing anyway and just move on ahead.

277
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:27,820
Scouts signing requirements for other scouts-

278
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:30,980
that's permitted to and it's good practice.

279
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,780
I will tell you this: getting a requirement signed

280
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,540
has nothing to do with anyone being tough

281
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:37,940
or anyone letting somebody else slide by on something.

282
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:39,260
I mean, what is advancement all about

283
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:41,740
Is: are we doing the whole advancement system

284
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:43,940
because it's especially important that

285
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:47,020
to the future, that our scouts

286
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:49,020
know how to build campfires and tie knots?

287
00:13:49,020 --> 00:13:51,660
If that's all we had in mind, it would be kind of silly.

288
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:54,260
We use advancement because, as I just spoke about,

289
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:57,900
it's a process through which our scouts grow

290
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:00,060
into these decent people that we wanna make,

291
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:02,020
who learn to think for themselves

292
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:05,140
and then develop an internal standard of honor and service.

293
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:08,180
The skills that we use as a part of this process

294
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:11,699
are really nowhere near as important as the process itself.

295
00:14:11,699 --> 00:14:13,819
When scouts sign requirements for other scouts,

296
00:14:13,819 --> 00:14:16,260
think about the kind of processes that work there.

297
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:18,860
Think about the interpersonal dynamics in play,

298
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:22,060
the kind of judgment and responsibility being practiced,

299
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:24,580
Something that is being denied to them

300
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,180
if adults are the only ones allowed

301
00:14:26,180 --> 00:14:28,420
to sign off requirements.

302
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:31,460
The skill and the level of skill isn't as important

303
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:34,860
as the process of learning and testing and judgment

304
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:36,340
and working with others.

305
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:38,700
That's why scouts should be signing requirements.

306
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:41,460
I hope that helps, and good on you again, Scott,

307
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:43,380
for being a good scout master

308
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,420
and using the patrol method.

309
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:48,460
Dawn is an adult volunteer with a scout troop in Virginia

310
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:49,900
and she wrote in to ask:

311
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:52,900
is it appropriate for Eagle Scout Master Conferences

312
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:55,700
to be in the private home of the scout master?

313
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,340
It just doesn't seem right to me.

314
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:58,940
Well, Dawn, thanks for getting in touch

315
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:02,740
and kudos for recognizing a potentially bad situation.

316
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:04,140
If you're an adult volunteer,

317
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:06,420
you've been through youth protection

318
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:09,460
and you hear that conferences are being held

319
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:11,340
at the scout master's home

320
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:14,420
and that may make you feel a little bit uneasy,

321
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:17,100
and that uneasy feeling should direct you

322
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:19,620
to make sure that things are above board

323
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:21,140
and being done properly.

324
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:23,900
If you go and look at the youth protection guidelines,

325
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:25,540
the simple answer to your question-

326
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:28,900
is it appropriate for an Eagle Scout Master Conference

327
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:31,420
to be held at the scout master's house?

328
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:34,260
You know, the simple answer is yes,

329
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:37,660
but there are some very important qualifications

330
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:38,940
to that answer.

331
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:41,220
Youth protection guidelines specify

332
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:45,900
that there is never to be any one-on-one contact

333
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:48,140
between an adult and a scout.

334
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:51,220
One-on-one contact is defined as a discussion or a meeting

335
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:55,860
or anything that is exclusively between an adult and a scout,

336
00:15:55,860 --> 00:15:58,780
not being observed or shared with a third person.

337
00:15:58,780 --> 00:16:01,420
If the scout is invited to the scout master's home

338
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:03,420
and the scout master's family is at home-

339
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,900
his wife or his children are at home,

340
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:08,940
or the scout is accompanied by a parent or a fellow scout

341
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:10,620
and the conversation takes place

342
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:12,940
where it can be observed by others,

343
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:15,180
It's within youth protection guidelines.

344
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:17,380
If those conditions aren't present,

345
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:19,020
then someone needs to report this

346
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,660
to their council executive.

347
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:23,500
That's right. just report it to the council executive,

348
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:24,660
Who will do all the work

349
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:26,620
that they are paid to do. at that point,

350
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:30,140
If you don't know exactly what's going on,

351
00:16:30,140 --> 00:16:31,660
I'd encourage you to ask the scout

352
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:33,340
or the scout master about this

353
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:35,700
and assure yourself that youth protection

354
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:38,860
is being followed. and that's a very simple question.

355
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:40,140
If you're talking to the scout,

356
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:43,220
say: I understand you visited Mr So-and-So's house

357
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:44,580
for your Eagle Conference.

358
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:46,540
Can you tell me who was there

359
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:48,819
And could you tell me where you had the Eagle Conference?

360
00:16:48,819 --> 00:16:51,500
Okay, and you can ask the scout master the same thing

361
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:54,380
You can say. I heard John came over to your house.

362
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,340
Were you two the only people at your house

363
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:57,740
or did he bring a buddy with him?

364
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:00,460
I don't think that those are improper questions to ask.

365
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:02,260
Good on you, Dawn, for having recognized

366
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:04,180
a potentially dangerous situation,

367
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:06,540
or just follow it through and check it up.

368
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:07,819
Nobody should ever be offended

369
00:17:07,819 --> 00:17:10,579
by somebody asking those sorts of questions,

370
00:17:10,579 --> 00:17:12,819
because we're all committed to youth protection

371
00:17:12,819 --> 00:17:15,379
and to following youth protection guidelines.

372
00:17:15,379 --> 00:17:16,540
If you wanna get in touch with me,

373
